  "question": {
    "text": "The integral $\\int \\frac{x d x}{2-x^2+\\sqrt{2-x^2}}$ equals :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "sOKot",
      "text": "\n$\\log \\left|1+\\sqrt{2+x^2}\\right|+c$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "K4HKF",
      "text": "\n$-\\log \\left|1+\\sqrt{2-x^2}\\right|+c$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "6LiVS",
      "text": "\n$-x \\log \\left|1-\\sqrt{2-x^2}\\right|+c$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "nm7hl",
      "text": "\n$x \\log \\left|1-\\sqrt{2+x^2}\\right|+c$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\quad \\mathrm{I}=\\int \\frac{x d x}{2-x^2+\\sqrt{2-x^2}}$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\text { Put } t=\\sqrt{2-x^2}, \\frac{d t}{d x}=\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{2-x^2}} \\cdot(-2 x) \\\\\n& \\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow-t d t=x d x \\\\\n& \\therefore \\\\\n& \\mathrm{I}=\\int \\frac{(-t) d t}{t^2+t}=-\\int \\frac{1}{t+1} d t=-\\log |t+1| \\\\\n&=-\\log \\left|\\sqrt{2-x^2}+1\\right|+c\n\\end{aligned}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
